{
  "method": "Built-in image_gen",
  "layout": "4 columns down/up/right/left, 2 rows A/B; transparent; 80px extracted frames",
  "template": "Create ONE production-ready pixel-art overworld walking sprite sheet for the SAME Gaon NAME shown in reference images. The references are the approved front and rear character designs, NOT sheet layouts. Preserve this exact species' anatomy, distinctive silhouette, colors, markings, clothing, accessories, face, ears, horns, tail and number of limbs. Do not redesign into a different animal. Make natural body-part animation, never just paste, stretch, shift or rotate the same static pose.\nOutput EXACTLY 8 separate complete sprites in a STRICT 4-column by 2-row grid of equal cells, with clear transparent gutters. Landscape 2:1 canvas preferred. Every cell contains this ONE creature only at identical scale, centered on the same local anchor. No text, no labels, no grid lines, no shadows, no ground, no effects outside sprite, no checkered backdrop. Genuinely transparent alpha background.\nColumns in BOTH rows, left to right:\n1 = FRONT facing DOWN toward viewer, face visible;\n2 = BACK facing UP away from viewer, rear body visible, no front face;\n3 = RIGHT side profile facing screen RIGHT, nose/head toward right;\n4 = LEFT side profile facing screen LEFT, nose/head toward left.\nRow 1 = movement pose A; Row 2 = complementary movement pose B.\nACTION\nUse a slightly elevated orthographic RPG map view, crisp square pixel clusters, dark readable outlines, clean limited palette shading matching reference. At least 12% padding within every cell, entire feet/wings/horns/tail visible. Consistent head/body size and baseline across all 8 frames. Both pose frames in each facing must clearly differ through natural movement of the creature's existing limbs/wings/fins/tail. Do not add nonexistent limbs.",
  "actions": {
    "walk": "Two-frame walking cycle: pose A advances left leg(s) and withdraws right leg(s); pose B advances right leg(s) and withdraws left. Existing arms and tail counter-swing naturally. Quadrupeds use alternating diagonal leg pairs; bipeds use two legs. Keep reference anatomy.",
    "fly": "Two-frame flight cycle: pose A wings clearly lifted and bent upward; pose B wings clearly swept downward and outward. Existing tail and feet counterbalance. Preserve wing shape, color pattern and feather count style.",
    "swim": "Two-frame swimming cycle: pose A bends tail/fin toward one side; pose B sweeps tail/fin to the opposite side. Fins paddle naturally; keep body volume stable. No added legs or water background.",
    "crawl": "Two-frame crawling cycle: existing legs alternate or, if a snail, its foot extends then contracts beneath a stable shell. Tentacles tilt slightly opposite between poses. No added legs to legless species.",
    "slither": "Two-frame slithering cycle: pose A body/tail bends into one natural S-curve; pose B bends into the complementary opposite curve. Head remains anchored, body volume and length stay consistent. No legs added.",
    "float": "Two-frame hovering cycle: existing arms, tendrils, flames, cloth or fins gently lift/open in pose A and relax/curl in pose B. Preserve exact anatomy and face. Do not merely translate or scale the whole sprite.",
    "hop": "Two-frame hopping cycle: pose A crouches/compresses naturally with feet tucked, pose B extends body and existing feet for a small hop. Preserve anatomy, proportions and recognizable face."
  },
